{"ts": 0.245841, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 4 · Commands and streams\u001b[0m \u001b[90m────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93m4.6\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 257}
{"ts": 0.245936, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mMany names at once\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 31}
{"ts": 0.245979, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n\u001b[92m*\u001b[0m matches any run of characters in a file name. The shell fills in\r\nthe names before the command runs.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mls *.txt\u001b[0m         \u001b[90m# every name ending in .txt\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mwc -l *.txt\u001b[0m      \u001b[90m# count the lines in each one\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA name with \u001b[92m*\u001b[0m in it is called a \u001b[1mglob\u001b[0m. Predict before you act: \u001b[92mrm *\u001b[0m\r\nwould remove everything in the folder.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try both, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for Stage 4's task.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 460}
