{"ts": 0.342814, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 4 · Commands and streams\u001b[0m \u001b[90m───────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93mtask\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 255}
{"ts": 0.342915, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mSTAGE 4 — GATE TASK\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 36}
{"ts": 0.343026, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "Do these:\r\n  1. Use \u001b[92mseq\u001b[0m and a pipe: count the lines of \u001b[92mseq 1 100\u001b[0m and\r\n     save that number to count.txt.\r\n  2. Use a glob to list every *.txt file in this folder.\r\n\r\nThen type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[0m.\r\n\u001b[90mI will check: count.txt exists and contains 100, and that you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mlisted the .txt files with a glob.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mThis task runs in /var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-uie1iel9/stage4; \u001b[92mpwd\u001b[90m shows it.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[93m when done.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 517}
{"ts": 0.345872, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mcheck\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(test your work)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(the task again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 132}
{"ts": 0.34617, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 253}
